  "schema:name": "Forest inventory, basal area (GeoCubes)",
  "schema:description": "The basal area of the growing stock on a forest stand is the cross section area of the tree stems of a stand per hectare and measured at a height of 1.3m, from the Multi-Source National Forest Inventory of Finland. Provided by LUKE. Scale: 10m-1000m. Coordinate system: ETRS-TM35FIN.",
